00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:08.030 align:start position:0%
if you thought Neos alpha demo was a bit  too challenging or maybe a little unfair  it sounds like the developers were  listening it's been a couple weeks since  the alpha demo period ended and now  developer team ninja has detailed what  it'll change for the final game the  changes are based on feedback it  received from an online survey and  includes improved exploration elements  the removal of weapon and armor  durability and a revamped stamina system  other changes will consist of improved  player and camera behavior while logged  on to an enemy and upgraded graphical  performance the full game will also  implement a training stage however the  exact details of all these changes are  still unclear additionally if you need  to free up some space on your hard drive  Team Ninja has said it's safe to delete  the game if you completed the demo  you'll still get the mark of the  Conqueror reward once the full game  launches Team Ninja also shared some  visuals that showed how different  regions reacted to the demo  interestingly the Japanese developed  game has received more positive feedback  from the Americas in Europe than Asia  for example difficulty in game balance  is marked as very good by thirty-seven  percent of respondents and goodbye  thirty five percent while Asia responded  with only eleven percent and twenty-two  percent respectively Yeoh releases for  the ps4 this year for a full list of the  changes check out the article on  gamespot com
 

